※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4538
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4538 LANG_IO_WITHOUT_A_DEVICE

※ A function that was handed no device may not read or write one.
※
※ Reaching a device through a *variable* is not being handed one: a variable at the
※ top level is ambient, so a function that writes through it is doing something its
※ signature does not account for and says so with `@[io]`.  The standard streams are
※ no such variable -- they arrive in `init.io` and are handed on by `&mut` -- but a
※ program may make one of its own, and this is what writing through it asks.
※
※ What it is *not* is `@[impure]`, and the note says which attribute would answer it.

let std := ⎕import("std")

let out: mut std.Writer = std.Writer(.fd ← 1i32)

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    ⎕drop(std.Io.println(&mut out, ⎕bytes("ambient")) ?? 0)
    0u6
